NAME
    cp - copy a file or directory

SYNOPSIS
    cp <src> <dst>
    cp -r <src> <dst>

DESCRIPTION
    Copies a real file. If <dst> is an existing directory, <src> lands
    inside it ('cp foo.txt logs/' -> 'logs/foo.txt'), matching real cp; an
    existing destination FILE is silently overwritten (no -i prompt anywhere
    in this shell, same as 'mv'). A directory requires -r, which copies it
    and everything inside it. Both <src> and <dst> must resolve inside the
    project's own directory tree - see 'cd'.

EXAMPLES
    cp notes.txt notes.bak.txt
    cp -r home/Logs/Run1 home/Logs/Run1Backup
